    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "479819a1_425a2c85",
        "filename": "baseboard/volteer/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T20:05:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This field(bits[25:23] \"product type as DFP\" is in PD 3.0 Rev3.0, while Rev 2.0 have those as reserved bits. Macro VDO_IDH defined in usb_pd.h doesn\u0027t have this field. Either we can update this macro to include this field(I think it needs a separate CL since it\u0027s used by multiple files); or I added a new macro like VDO_IDH_REV3 in usb_pd_vdo.h.",
      "parentUuid": "8db0d123_0db42758",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b171a1885d58cc839f6a134d362b646dffe1cce5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93933db2_7fb3911f",
        "filename": "baseboard/volteer/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T20:40:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since there is a difference between Rev2.0 and Rev3.0, we need to change our response here based on what version the protocol we\u0027re running. If our partner is PD 2.0, we need to not set this field. Probably, that logic should be in svdm_tbt_compat_response_identity for now, and there should be const structures for each revision.\n\nThere may be other issues of this type implicated in this CL that I\u0027m unaware of.\n\nWRT code style, I\u0027m not fond of these types of macros (as opposed to functions), because they make this kind of thing awkward to deal with. I\u0027d like to be able to have a function that takes all field values for all the revisions, along with the currently operation revision for the partner, and returns a well-typed VDO.\n\nProbably the easiest thing to do for now would be add another macro. I know our VDO stuff is scattered all over the place, but it should probably be in usb_pd.h, next to VDO_IDH. Sigh.",
      "parentUuid": "479819a1_425a2c85",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b171a1885d58cc839f6a134d362b646dffe1cce5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0887eb37_eee8c9cd",
        "filename": "baseboard/volteer/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-21T15:58:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added a Rev3.0 macro to create a const for Rev3.0, and select proper VDO based on port PD Rev. I don\u0027t see a common function between TCPMv1\u0026v2 to get PD revision on a port.  pd_get_rev() is the one in TCPMv1 and prl_get_rev() is the one in TCPMv2. I uploaded CL:2420468 to address this.",
      "parentUuid": "93933db2_7fb3911f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b171a1885d58cc839f6a134d362b646dffe1cce5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
